{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.BringFigureEightDepth2Witness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BringFigureEightDepth2Witness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BringFigureEightDepth2Witness.not_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BringFigureEightDepth2Witness.not_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BringFigureEightDepth2Witness.lean#L150-L155","doc":"**Inhabitation depends on the data** — the property the old schema lacked\nentirely. Here is data at which the class is **refutable**: two sides that\ndiffer. Under the previous shape no choice of anything could fail, so a wrong\nidentification had nothing to fail against. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BringFigureEightDepth2Witness.nonempty_of_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BringFigureEightDepth2Witness.nonempty_of_eq","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BringFigureEightDepth2Witness.lean#L145-L148","doc":"**Not over-corrected**: inhabited whenever the two sides agree, so the class\nbeing open is not an artefact of its being empty. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BringFigureEightDepth2Witness.evaluates_to","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BringFigureEightDepth2Witness.evaluates_to","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BringFigureEightDepth2Witness.lean#L124-L135","doc":"**The conjecture composed with the verified evaluation.**\n\n`hClosedForm` is the numerically discharged half — `std(2 Im Li₂^q(e^{iπ/3})) =\n2 Cl₂(π/3)`, established to 50 digits by the block's committed witness, not by\nthis file. Supplying it as a hypothesis rather than a field is what keeps the\ntwo halves' provenance distinct: the instance carries the conjecture, the\nargument carries the computation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BringFigureEightDepth2Witness.identifies","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BringFigureEightDepth2Witness.identifies","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BringFigureEightDepth2Witness.lean#L106-L106","doc":"**The conjecture**: the structural identification of the volume with the\ndepth-2 grouplike value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BringFigureEightDepth2Witness.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BringFigureEightDepth2Witness.mk","kind":"ctor","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BringFigureEightDepth2Witness.lean#L103-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BringFigureEightDepth2Witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BringFigureEightDepth2Witness","kind":"class","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BringFigureEightDepth2Witness.lean#L83-L106","doc":"**Bring figure-8 volume as a depth-2 grouplike value.**\n\nThe conjecture of\n[`conj:bring-figure-eight-depth-2-witness`](../../../mass-theory/bring-figure-eight-depth-2-witness.md):\nthe hyperbolic volume of the figure-8 knot equals the standard part of the\ndepth-2 grouplike value at the regular-ideal-tetrahedron shape parameter.\n\nParameters are the caller's data:\n\n* `figureEightVolume` — `Vol(S³ \\ 4₁)`, the archimedean side;\n* `grouplikeStd` — `std(2 Im Li₂^q(e^{iπ/3}))`, the algebraic side.\n\nBoth sides carry Goncharov period-depth 2 and iterated-integral depth 2\nrespectively. That match is **not** a field: the block derives it \"by\nconstruction of the Bloch–Wigner regulator\", so it is a fact the conjecture is\nstated against, not part of what the conjecture asserts.\n\nAn instance **is** the conjecture, for that data. None is provided, and an\ninstance would still not discharge `conj:gb-depth-period-correspondence` — see\nthe header. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:bring-figure-eight-depth-2-witness","label":"conj:bring-figure-eight-depth-2-witness","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/bring-figure-eight-depth-2-witness.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}